<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n104280" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοξ-άζομαι</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τόξον</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>shoot with a bow,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				8.220
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				228
			</span></i>: c. gen. objecti, <i>shoot at,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰ καὶ . . τοξαζοίατο φωτῶν</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				218
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κακῶς ἀνδρῶν τοξάζεαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					22.27
				</span></i>
			: later c. acc., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. θῆρας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Opp.
					<u>C.</u>
					4.54
				</span></i>
			.—Poet. word, for which <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοξεύω</span> is usual in Prose, but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοξάζω</span> (
				Act.
			) occurs in <i><span class="en">
				Heraclit.
				<u>All.</u>
				13
			</span></i>.</div>
